Date: August 16, 2026
Project: Khaemenes Academy / Verve N Veda
Scope: Pre-K through Grade 08, Academy continuity, NAIB delegation, Archaemenes mentoring, learner records, certification, and Middle School transition architecture

Overview

Today’s work focused on unifying the learner-continuity architecture across Khaemenes Academy and hardening the educational progression from Preschool through Middle School.

The central goal was not to rewrite the curriculum. The curriculum itself was preserved wherever it was already strong. Instead, the work concentrated on identity authority, mentor continuity, NAIB delegation, learner-scoped records, adult verification, certification rules, legacy migration safety, and transitions between school stages.

The emerging Academy-wide model is:

Academy Family Registry
        ↓
NAIB intake / resource direction / delegation
        ↓
Khaemenes Academy
        ↓
Archaemenes · institutional Academy mentor
        ↓
Developmental / grade / course context
        ↓
Assessment evidence
        ↓
Adult verification
        ↓
Learner-scoped formal record
        ↓
Certificate / readiness / transition

This architecture is intended to remain consistent as the Academy grows upward into High School and Higher Learning.

1. Canonical Intelligence & Mentoring Architecture

NAIB

NAIB is now treated consistently as the Academy ecosystem’s:

front-desk administrator;

AI Resources Director;

intake layer;

intent interpreter;

delegation intelligence;

resource and destination router.

NAIB receives a visitor’s context and determines where that person should go.

A destination can be:

Khaemenes Academy;

a school stage;

a specialist AI platform;

a game or practice resource;

a knowledge or research resource;

a civic resource;

an emergency resource;

the 333 communications hub;

a family-account resource;

a Higher Learning pathway;

another Verve N Veda platform.

Canonical wording:

NAIB receives, interprets, delegates, and connects.

NAIB does not become the permanent academic mentor.

Archaemenes

Archaemenes is the institutional AI mentor of Khaemenes Academy.

Developmental presentation changes by stage, but identity does not.

Examples:

Preschool / early stages — child-appropriate presentation;

Elementary — Young Scholar;

Middle School — Academy Scholar.

Archaemenes:

mentors;

helps organize thinking;

provides hints and learning guidance;

supports evidence-based reasoning;

does not grade;

does not award mastery;

does not control formal promotion.

Specialist AIs

Other specialist platforms retain their own specialist AIs.

Examples already established:

MoirAI — The Refrain music mentor;

Eiren — language arts / literary mentor;

Archaemenes — Khaemenes Academy mentor.

A learner may interact with multiple specialist AIs depending on platform and subject.

The Family Registry therefore must not treat one mentorId as a permanent global learner authority.

