5. Multi-Learner Legacy Migration Repair

During validation, an important cross-grade issue was identified.

Older shared localStorage records could potentially be rewritten with the latest learner’s state. That created a risk that a second sibling or learner using the same browser could inherit a previous learner’s compatibility snapshot.

This was corrected across Grades 01–05.

The hardened approach now uses:

learner-scoped formal record storage;

read-only historical legacy keys;

one-time migration claims;

no rewriting of the old shared record;

protection against silent multi-learner migration.

This was one of the most important integrity fixes completed today.

