14. Advanced Learner / Accelerated Trajectory Design

The next improvement should support learners who are ready to work above nominal grade level without corrupting formal placement.

The correct model should be:

Formal Academy placement
        ≠
Learning access / advanced resource access

A Grade 05 learner may remain formally:

stage: elementary
grade: grade-05

while receiving access to:

Grade 06 preview material;

advanced mathematics;

advanced reading;

research;

science;

projects;

Middle School resource sampling;

readiness diagnostics;

challenge tracks.

This allows acceleration without silently rewriting the learner’s grade.

Proposed Advanced Bridge Model

Grade 05 learner
    ↓
Adult / Academy readiness review
    ↓
Advanced pathway flag or recommendation
    ↓
NAIB delegation to approved Middle School preview resources
    ↓
Archaemenes continues mentoring
    ↓
Formal Grade 05 placement remains unchanged
    ↓
Promotion occurs only through explicit Academy / family action

This should become a deliberate “Advanced Pathway” rather than an automatic promotion mechanism.

